# Enforce LF line endings for all text files in the working tree.
#
# The generator scripts (generate-cards, generate-csp-meta, generate-sitemap, …)
# emit LF. With core.autocrlf=true, Git would otherwise check text files out as
# CRLF on Windows, so the freshly-generated LF blocks drift against the rest of
# the (CRLF) file and the generate-cards "no drift" test fails. `eol=lf` here
# wins over autocrlf and keeps the working tree byte-for-byte consistent with
# what the generators produce. The repo already stores LF, so this introduces
# no renormalization churn in the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize line endings.
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf   binary
